class Solution {
    Node prev = null;                                                      // Tracks previously visited node in inorder
    
    Node bToDLL(Node root) {

        if(root == null){ return null;}                                    // Base case: null node
        
        Node head = bToDLL(root.left);                                     // Recursively convert left subtree
        
        if(prev == null){ head = root; }                                   // First node (leftmost) = head
        
        else{
            root.left = prev;                                              // Link current to previous (prev -> current)
            prev.right = root;                                             // Link previous to current (current -> prev)
        }
        
        prev = root;                                                       // Update prev to current node
        
        bToDLL(root.right);                                                // Recursively convert right subtree
        
        return head;                                                       // Return head of DLL
                
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Example: root = [10, 20, 30, 40, 60]

       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \
   40  60

Inorder: 40 → 20 → 60 → 10 → 30

bToDLL(10):
  bToDLL(20):
    bToDLL(40): prev=null → head=40, prev=40
    20.left=40, 40.right=20, prev=20
    bToDLL(60): 60.left=20, 20.right=60, prev=60
    → returns head=40
  10.left=60, 60.right=10, prev=10
  bToDLL(30): 30.left=10, 10.right=30, prev=30
  → returns head=40

DLL: 40 ⇄ 20 ⇄ 60 ⇄ 10 ⇄ 30
Output: [40, 20, 60, 10, 30]

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Binary Tree to DLL
Given the root of a binary tree, convert it to a Doubly Linked List (DLL) in place.
- Use left pointer as prev and right pointer as next
- Form DLL using inorder traversal (Left → Root → Right)
- The leftmost node becomes head
- Return head of DLL

Examples:

----------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [1, 2, 3]
Output: [2, 1, 3]
       1
      / \
     2   3

Explanation: Inorder: 2 → 1 → 3, DLL: 2 ⇄ 1 ⇄ 3

----------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [10, 20, 30, 40, 60]

       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \
   40  60

Output: [40, 20, 60, 10, 30]
Explanation: Inorder: 40 → 20 → 60 → 10 → 30, DLL: 40 ⇄ 20 ⇄ 60 ⇄ 10 ⇄ 30

----------------------------------------------------------------

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ Number of nodes ≤ 10^5
• 0 ≤ Data of a node ≤ 10^5

